# Central pinned refs for vanilla_wow_lab player builds.
#
# One source of truth so wowborg always layers on the SAME deployed shim. Sourced by
# tools/build_player.sh and passed to wowborg/Dockerfile as --build-arg. Pattern follows
# crewrift_lab/tools/versions.env; rationale in
# docs/designs/wowborg-v2-shim-adoption.md ("Image: layer on the deployed artifact").

# The DEPLOYED reference player image wowborg layers on (the "shim"): the exact bytes
# the league runs — king_richard + wow_sdk (nim_control) + the vanilla_wow_coworld.player
# WS wrapper. NOTE (0.1.31+): the player image no longer bundles world data or the
# navmesh helper — the GAME container serves Maps/VMaps/MMaps/DBC over an authenticated
# HTTP asset endpoint, passed to the child as an --assets=<url> argument.
#
# DELIBERATELY A DIGEST, not a tag — tags move, digests don't. Provenance:
#   vanilla_wow package 0.1.31 (cow_e8eef946-2010-4cca-8b18-6752c110b3dd),
#   fetched 2026-07-21 via `uv run coworld download vanilla_wow`.
# How to bump: a new vanilla_wow version appears in `coworld list` (the live manifest is
# the truth — trust it over the game-repo checkout). Then:
#   1. `coworld download vanilla_wow`; read the player-image digest from coworld_images.json
#      (the image whose manifest player entries run `vanilla-wow-reference-player`).
#   2. Update this pin.
#   3. Re-extract the SDK snapshot the bridge tests validate against (recipe in
#      wowborg/tests/conftest.py) — the control contract is strict (extra="forbid")
#      on BOTH sides and drifts (0.1.19→0.1.31 replaced the whole action seam).
#   4. Rebuild + rerun tests; a contract drift fails loudly.
# Prior pin: 0.1.19 sha256:665adff0… (file-bridge/action.json era; superseded 2026-07-21).
WOWBORG_BASE_IMAGE=public.ecr.aws/q5f4m8t9/cogames@sha256:8ebfdec6e0ce92c41202c61b0163ffa49cd80a32ddce39606931dd73eaf8fd6f
